
  <sn><md>### Understaning

The easiest way to understand them is: 
- `editor` edits Git messages,
- `diff` compares, 
- `difftool` visually compares and
- `mergetool` resolves conflicts

| Command/tool    | Purpose                              | Opens GUI? | Typical use                                     |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------ | ---------: | ----------------------------------------------- |
| **Git editor**      | Edit Git-generated text              |    Depends | Write commit/merge/rebase messages              |
| `git diff`      | Show differences                     |          ❌ | Inspect code changes `only in terminal`                |
| `git difftool`  | Show differences using a visual tool |          ✅ | Compare files in Sublime Merge                  |
| `git mergetool` | Resolve merge conflicts              |          ✅ | Decide how conflicting files should be combined |
</md></sn>
